WEBVTT

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:03.980
<b>Inter-High Road Race Boys' Champions</b>

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:07.440
<b>Makishima Yusuke</b>

00:00:21.710 --> 00:00:23.270
Makishima-san...

00:00:24.030 --> 00:00:26.290
<i>Why do you look so dejected,</i>

00:00:26.290 --> 00:00:28.210
Sakamichi?

00:00:40.730 --> 00:00:42.020
<i>I wonder why?</i>

00:00:42.850 --> 00:00:46.820
<i>Lately, I've been able to recall 
so clearly the feeling of him</i>

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:50.020
<i>slapping me on the back.</i>

00:00:51.980 --> 00:00:53.230
No, no!

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:59.830
Makishima-san asked me 
to make Sohoku stronger.

00:01:00.450 --> 00:01:03.080
We're counting on you to carry our Sohoku.

00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:07.960
<i>That's why I can't lose heart.</i>

00:01:08.690 --> 00:01:12.380
<i>I have to shake off the 
past and move forward.</i>

00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:15.260
I'm taking the lead!

00:01:43.830 --> 00:01:46.410
<b><i>Yowamushi Pedal</i></b>

00:02:57.380 --> 00:03:01.630
<i>RIDE.2 What Makishima Left Behind</i>

00:02:57.990 --> 00:03:00.530
Onoda-kun, you've been falling a lot lately.

00:03:00.930 --> 00:03:02.770
Are you sure you're not being overeager?

00:03:02.770 --> 00:03:03.860
Are you hurt?

00:03:03.860 --> 00:03:06.980
N-No, I'm fine.

00:03:06.980 --> 00:03:09.480
You're always diving into the grass.

00:03:09.480 --> 00:03:12.120
Are you still not used to your bike?

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:15.870
Y-Yeah, that's it.

00:03:15.870 --> 00:03:18.300
Riding a new bike sure is hard.

00:03:18.870 --> 00:03:21.880
It's too light, and the brakes work too well.

00:03:24.970 --> 00:03:27.700
Can I refill my water bottle at 
the vending machine up ahead?

00:03:27.700 --> 00:03:28.910
Yeah, same.

00:03:32.940 --> 00:03:34.070
Teshima-san...

00:03:34.780 --> 00:03:36.560
Is this about Makishima-san?

00:03:36.560 --> 00:03:37.150
Huh?

00:03:38.150 --> 00:03:41.150
Makishima is quitting the team today.

00:03:43.390 --> 00:03:45.050
N-No...

00:03:45.050 --> 00:03:47.160
Really? That's fine, then.

00:03:47.790 --> 00:03:50.990
It's dangerous to practice 
while lost in thought.

00:03:50.990 --> 00:03:52.160
Be careful.

00:03:52.160 --> 00:03:53.040
Yes, sir.

00:03:53.780 --> 00:03:58.670
Now that Makishima-san is gone, 
you're Sohoku's only climber.

00:04:03.650 --> 00:04:07.300
Shall we sprint to the top, like usual?

00:04:07.300 --> 00:04:08.640
Yeah!

00:04:09.030 --> 00:04:11.290
It's just a 200 meter slope.

00:04:11.290 --> 00:04:14.430
That's short enough to sprint up.

00:04:14.430 --> 00:04:15.560
Don't push yourself too hard.

00:04:16.140 --> 00:04:19.150
<i>A slope? Climbing?</i>

00:04:19.580 --> 00:04:22.150
<i>That's right. I...</i>

00:04:22.150 --> 00:04:24.950
<i>I have to work harder.</i>

00:04:32.830 --> 00:04:34.430
<i>My power...</i>

00:04:34.850 --> 00:04:37.380
<i>It's no use. I can't get any power.</i>

00:04:46.990 --> 00:04:47.590
Onoda...

00:04:49.240 --> 00:04:52.660
Sorry, Teshima-san! Er, Captain!

00:04:52.660 --> 00:04:56.100
You must be here to ask me what I'm 
doing when I'm supposed to be a climber.

00:04:56.590 --> 00:04:59.610
I... I'll get my head back 
on straight and climb!

00:05:00.200 --> 00:05:02.890
No, it's fine. Let's take it slow.

00:05:02.890 --> 00:05:03.510
Huh?

00:05:04.140 --> 00:05:05.360
The weather's nice.

00:05:07.700 --> 00:05:09.340
Does it hurt, Onoda?

00:05:09.900 --> 00:05:13.290
Despite how he looked, 
Makishima-san was a nice guy.

00:05:14.150 --> 00:05:16.710
When we were first-years...

00:05:16.960 --> 00:05:20.850
You want me to give you tips on climbing?

00:05:20.850 --> 00:05:23.340
Well...

00:05:23.890 --> 00:05:27.010
Swing your bike back and forth really hard.

00:05:27.010 --> 00:05:29.710
You're the only one who can do that!

00:05:29.710 --> 00:05:31.060
Oh, really?

00:05:32.260 --> 00:05:34.390
He was always kind.

00:05:35.170 --> 00:05:36.790
I still...

00:05:37.390 --> 00:05:41.150
I still had a lot to learn!

00:05:41.150 --> 00:05:42.750
So why...

00:05:44.570 --> 00:05:46.350
If you're hurting, you can rest.

00:05:47.810 --> 00:05:50.370
Forcing yourself to practice 
now won't help you.

00:05:50.710 --> 00:05:51.950
Remember what he said.

00:05:51.950 --> 00:05:54.950
When you aim for the top, 
you learn where you stand.

00:05:55.400 --> 00:05:59.960
Choosing your course of action based 
on how others see you or think of you

00:05:59.960 --> 00:06:02.470
won't get you anywhere.

00:06:03.630 --> 00:06:04.840
I'm weak.

00:06:05.150 --> 00:06:07.270
Naruko and Imaizumi are strong.

00:06:07.940 --> 00:06:10.810
They fought as equals alongside the 
third-years during the Inter-High.

00:06:11.390 --> 00:06:14.980
Aoyagi and I still don't stand a 
chance against them in sprints.

00:06:14.980 --> 00:06:17.090
Even though I'm the captain, 
I'm the weakest one.

00:06:17.090 --> 00:06:18.560
I'm not strong mentally, either.

00:06:19.770 --> 00:06:22.560
But I know that.

00:06:23.130 --> 00:06:27.070
What I need to do is make up for 
those weaknesses little by little.

00:06:27.420 --> 00:06:29.390
That's where I'll find my breakthrough.

00:06:29.390 --> 00:06:30.530
That's what I believe.

00:06:31.320 --> 00:06:35.240
You can rest. You can worry, Onoda.

00:06:35.710 --> 00:06:38.030
Even that can be a way to move forward.

00:06:38.890 --> 00:06:42.170
Believe in yourself. You'll find the light.

00:06:42.950 --> 00:06:46.280
Didn't Makishima-san entrust 
his soul to you, too?

00:06:52.510 --> 00:06:53.290
Yeah.

00:06:54.900 --> 00:06:57.930
<i>AIR Airlines flight 1602 is...</i>

00:06:57.930 --> 00:07:01.170
Jeez. I'm about to get on a plane.

00:07:01.170 --> 00:07:04.600
Why'd you have to call 
me last minute, Toudou?

00:07:06.310 --> 00:07:08.130
<i>My friend's embarking on a voyage.</i>

00:07:08.130 --> 00:07:09.900
<i>I thought I should congratulate you.</i>

00:07:10.240 --> 00:07:11.810
<i>Besides, you're alone, aren't you?</i>

00:07:11.810 --> 00:07:13.060
Well, yeah.

00:07:13.570 --> 00:07:17.580
I told them to practice if 
they had time to see me off.

00:07:19.030 --> 00:07:22.950
We lost this year, but we'll 
win next year, Maki-chan.

00:07:22.950 --> 00:07:24.290
Even after I graduate,

00:07:24.290 --> 00:07:29.540
<i>Hakone will have plenty of other strong
climbers like Kuroda and Manami.</i>

00:07:30.580 --> 00:07:32.620
<i>You've only got Four-Eyes, right?</i>

00:07:33.090 --> 00:07:36.290
No matter how strong he is, 
he can't win by himself.

00:07:37.530 --> 00:07:41.140
No, we've got climbers.

00:07:41.140 --> 00:07:43.520
Really? Are they strong?

00:07:43.520 --> 00:07:44.650
Do they have good instincts?

00:07:48.100 --> 00:07:49.530
Not at all.

00:07:49.530 --> 00:07:50.990
What?

00:07:50.990 --> 00:07:56.240
But maybe that's Sohoku's type.

00:07:56.240 --> 00:07:59.540
No talent and no instinct...

00:07:59.540 --> 00:08:03.750
So he climbs through sheer effort.

00:08:10.500 --> 00:08:15.300
<i>Makishima-san said he could make this 
climb in six minutes at his fastest.</i>

00:08:17.790 --> 00:08:21.270
<i>He's a monster, but...</i>

00:08:21.990 --> 00:08:25.220
<i>I'll catch up to him, even if it's 
only by one second, one centimeter!</i>

00:08:26.420 --> 00:08:28.900
Teshima, you're a climber.

00:08:28.900 --> 00:08:29.830
What?

00:08:29.830 --> 00:08:32.430
Tricks don't work on climbs.

00:08:32.430 --> 00:08:37.870
Unlike flats, you can't hide behind 
other riders to get out of the wind.

00:08:38.350 --> 00:08:44.790
Your weakness can't be overcome 
with knowledge or technique.

00:08:45.300 --> 00:08:46.600
So climb.

00:08:48.380 --> 00:08:51.460
<i>Keep climbing until your legs stop moving.</i>

00:08:52.020 --> 00:08:53.020
<i>I'll do it.</i>

00:08:53.020 --> 00:08:57.470
<i>Even if it's impossible,
I'll push myself to the limit.</i>

00:08:58.330 --> 00:09:01.600
<i>I can at least push myself 
as close as possible!</i>

00:09:02.710 --> 00:09:04.260
<i>I will become stronger!</i>

00:09:14.950 --> 00:09:18.030
<i>Yesterday my best time was eight minutes.</i>

00:09:19.790 --> 00:09:21.580
<i>Six minutes is still far away.</i>

00:09:22.260 --> 00:09:24.430
Teshima, I heard the news.

00:09:25.040 --> 00:09:26.030
Higashida.

00:09:26.030 --> 00:09:28.170
You're the captain of the bike club now?

00:09:28.170 --> 00:09:30.050
Yeah.

00:09:30.050 --> 00:09:32.740
The team's strong, right? 
I heard you won nationals.

00:09:33.220 --> 00:09:34.840
That must be a lot of pressure.

00:09:35.170 --> 00:09:37.420
Every day I feel like puking.

00:09:37.420 --> 00:09:39.930
The first-years are so strong,
I can't keep up.

00:09:40.310 --> 00:09:41.610
How's the volleyball club?

00:09:42.060 --> 00:09:44.790
Unfortunately, we only made 
it to the second round.

00:09:44.790 --> 00:09:47.550
Because of that,
our practices are hellish now.

00:09:47.550 --> 00:09:48.100
How about you?

00:09:48.570 --> 00:09:50.030
It's hard.

00:09:50.030 --> 00:09:52.800
It makes me realize the difference 
between being made to do something

00:09:52.800 --> 00:09:54.120
and making yourself do something.

00:09:54.120 --> 00:09:57.110
I was just coming up with the 
lineup for our next race.

00:09:57.110 --> 00:10:03.080
<b>Training
Sprinting
Climbing
Long Rides</b>

00:09:57.110 --> 00:10:03.080
<b>Practice

00:09:57.110 --> 00:10:03.080
<b>September
October</b>

00:09:57.610 --> 00:10:00.020
There's a lot to do as the captain.

00:10:00.020 --> 00:10:03.080
Practice, paperwork, and other stuff.

00:10:03.750 --> 00:10:05.450
When I think about how 
Kinjou-senpai used to do this,

00:10:05.450 --> 00:10:07.190
it makes me realize how tough he really was.

00:10:07.190 --> 00:10:11.370
Want to go karaoke after practice, then?

00:10:11.370 --> 00:10:12.130
What?

00:10:12.630 --> 00:10:16.740
I've been planning it since I 
heard you became the captain.

00:10:16.740 --> 00:10:19.720
Let me hear that Teshima medley again.

00:10:20.500 --> 00:10:24.180
I got together the guys we rode 
with in middle school, too.

00:10:24.940 --> 00:10:26.730
Everyone wants to congratulate you.

00:10:27.390 --> 00:10:29.650
You once said you were quitting,

00:10:29.650 --> 00:10:33.570
and now you're the captain of 
the team that won nationals.

00:10:36.500 --> 00:10:37.610
Teshima!

00:10:37.610 --> 00:10:40.500
Why? You can't quit!

00:10:40.500 --> 00:10:42.120
Don't you like riding your bike?

00:10:42.120 --> 00:10:44.950
We swore we'd win together.

00:10:46.730 --> 00:10:47.870
Oh, right.

00:10:47.870 --> 00:10:52.010
I invited Iwase-chan from the 
girls' volleyball team,

00:10:52.010 --> 00:10:53.810
who you said you were interested in.

00:10:54.750 --> 00:10:58.720
When I told her about your medley of 
impressions, she said yes right away.

00:11:07.110 --> 00:11:10.480
Sorry, but I don't have time.

00:11:11.730 --> 00:11:12.810
Really?

00:11:14.700 --> 00:11:16.060
That's too bad.

00:11:16.930 --> 00:11:18.020
Thanks.

00:11:19.470 --> 00:11:22.950
<i>Sorry, Higashida. I wish I could go.</i>

00:11:23.710 --> 00:11:27.700
<i>But when I closed my eyes, I saw...</i>

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:32.140
<i>...Onoda at the Inter-High.</i>

00:11:34.210 --> 00:11:36.110
<i>Am I stupid?</i>

00:11:37.340 --> 00:11:42.270
<i>But my heart belongs to the Inter-High.</i>

00:11:43.870 --> 00:11:47.790
<i>We'll stand there again. 
We are the champions.</i>

00:11:48.200 --> 00:11:52.690
<i>We'll ride through three searingly 
hot days and stand on that stage.</i>

00:11:55.330 --> 00:11:56.900
<b><i>Minegayama Hill Climb</i></b>

00:11:55.810 --> 00:12:00.460
These contain essential information 
and regulations for our next race.

00:12:00.460 --> 00:12:02.380
Could you hand them out to the first-years?

00:12:02.380 --> 00:12:02.990
Yes, sir.

00:12:03.910 --> 00:12:06.380
<i>Teshima-san's in a good mood.</i>

00:12:07.120 --> 00:12:09.500
How has Onoda been doing?

00:12:09.940 --> 00:12:11.900
He stopped falling.

00:12:11.900 --> 00:12:16.750
He's still slow, but he seems to 
be getting used to his new bike.

00:12:17.820 --> 00:12:18.860
That's great.

00:12:20.350 --> 00:12:21.740
Little by little is fine.

00:12:21.740 --> 00:12:23.300
Let him know I said that.

00:12:24.510 --> 00:12:25.950
<i>Little by little...</i>

00:12:25.950 --> 00:12:28.470
<i>Little by little, it's taking shape.</i>

00:12:29.220 --> 00:12:32.230
<i>With the third-years leaving, 
the lineup has changed.</i>

00:12:33.220 --> 00:12:35.090
<i>Makishima-san is gone, but...</i>

00:12:38.500 --> 00:12:39.230
Junta...

00:12:39.580 --> 00:12:40.690
Aoyagi.

00:12:41.170 --> 00:12:43.150
How did yesterday go?

00:12:43.720 --> 00:12:45.910
I attacked just before the 200 meter mark.

00:12:51.340 --> 00:12:53.780
I knew you'd come, so I've 
been saving my strength.

00:12:53.780 --> 00:12:55.740
Pedal with all you've got, Aoyagi!

00:12:56.700 --> 00:12:57.420
Yes, sir!

00:13:08.710 --> 00:13:09.550
I won.

00:13:10.810 --> 00:13:12.860
All right! That's great!

00:13:12.860 --> 00:13:14.770
But I've still only won once.

00:13:14.770 --> 00:13:15.890
That's fine.

00:13:16.580 --> 00:13:19.980
<i>Imaizumi, Naruko, Onoda, Aoyagi...</i>

00:13:20.590 --> 00:13:25.900
<i>The second generation of Sohoku is 
moving forward, one step at a time.</i>

00:13:28.260 --> 00:13:33.750
Hakone Academy's next captain 
will be Izumida Touichirou.

00:13:34.170 --> 00:13:34.830
Yes, sir.

00:13:35.700 --> 00:13:38.380
Jeez, this ceremony is a pain in the ass.

00:13:38.810 --> 00:13:42.120
All you need to do is win.

00:13:42.120 --> 00:13:45.560
With a man who went through that bitter 
experience at the Inter-High as captain,

00:13:45.560 --> 00:13:46.220
we can't lose.

00:13:46.220 --> 00:13:48.630
You're a perfect fit, Izumida.

00:13:48.630 --> 00:13:54.470
The next generation of Hakone Academy 
will led by the three second-years.

00:13:55.370 --> 00:13:56.330
Three?

00:13:57.100 --> 00:14:02.210
The vice-captain will be 
second-year Kuroda Yukinari.

00:14:02.860 --> 00:14:08.680
<i>This year I lost to Manami in the 
qualifier despite our promise.</i>

00:14:10.120 --> 00:14:11.890
<i>But next year will be different.</i>

00:14:12.750 --> 00:14:16.740
Touichirou, let's go wild 
at the next Inter-High.

00:14:17.250 --> 00:14:18.120
Yuki!

00:14:27.610 --> 00:14:30.710
Captain Izumida and vice-captain Kuroda...

00:14:31.400 --> 00:14:34.310
These two were obvious 
choices for their positions.

00:14:34.730 --> 00:14:39.420
But I'm surprised you recommended 
him for the third, Shinkai.

00:14:39.420 --> 00:14:41.000
He's promising.

00:14:41.000 --> 00:14:42.790
Don't you agree?

00:14:45.230 --> 00:14:50.110
From Chiba Minami Middle School, 
he moved here for his parents' work.

00:14:50.590 --> 00:14:56.470
Apparently he was on the same middle school 
team as Sohoku's next captain, Teshima-kun.

00:14:56.470 --> 00:14:58.870
Excuse me, Shinkai-san.

00:15:01.540 --> 00:15:04.680
My jersey's a little small.

00:15:05.130 --> 00:15:06.880
Second-year Ashikiba Takuto...

00:15:07.240 --> 00:15:11.130
He's Hakone Academy's tallest 
member ever, at 202 centimeters.

00:15:13.510 --> 00:15:17.450
Ashikiba, what was Teshima-kun 
like in middle school?

00:15:18.170 --> 00:15:19.940
Him?

00:15:21.160 --> 00:15:22.810
He's good.

00:15:22.810 --> 00:15:24.660
Good, huh?

00:15:25.150 --> 00:15:27.090
Yeah, at karaoke.

00:15:28.810 --> 00:15:32.300
His medley of impressions 
is truly exceptional.

00:15:32.780 --> 00:15:35.240
Ow...

00:15:36.710 --> 00:15:37.760
Heave-ho...

00:15:37.760 --> 00:15:39.320
Don't, Ashikiba!

00:15:39.320 --> 00:15:41.410
I won't be able to get my bike down!

00:15:41.720 --> 00:15:42.730
Ashikiba...

00:15:43.750 --> 00:15:47.000
How would you like to 
race against Teshima-kun?

00:15:47.380 --> 00:15:51.170
A race? I can race already?

00:15:52.610 --> 00:15:56.250
Okay. If that's what you want, 
I'll give it everything I've got.

00:15:56.250 --> 00:16:00.780
Basically, you want me to 
beat him in that race, right?

00:16:03.310 --> 00:16:06.480
No, you don't have to worry about that.

00:16:07.240 --> 00:16:10.650
Someone else will be 
participating in that race.

00:16:11.240 --> 00:16:13.240
<b>Meeting In Progress
Do Not Enter</b>

00:16:13.720 --> 00:16:18.030
Our methods weren't wrong.

00:16:18.610 --> 00:16:21.120
Arakita and Izumida pulled ahead of them.

00:16:21.780 --> 00:16:24.150
Shinkai pulled us through the flats.

00:16:24.590 --> 00:16:27.730
Then we sent our climbers.

00:16:28.980 --> 00:16:34.670
Toudou kept Makishima in check,
leaving Manami and me.

00:16:35.310 --> 00:16:37.170
Almost everything went according to plan.

00:16:37.690 --> 00:16:41.220
But Sohoku faced problem after problem.

00:16:42.640 --> 00:16:44.020
Their ace, Kinjou, was injured.

00:16:44.450 --> 00:16:45.770
He fell behind immediately.

00:16:47.140 --> 00:16:50.190
Their ace switched to an 
inexperienced first-year.

00:16:52.010 --> 00:16:54.900
We had an overwhelming advantage.

00:16:54.900 --> 00:16:56.490
But we lost!

00:16:56.490 --> 00:16:59.750
But not because we underestimated them.

00:16:59.750 --> 00:17:00.370
What?

00:17:00.370 --> 00:17:02.830
We totally underestimated them.

00:17:03.540 --> 00:17:07.250
Although I can't imagine 
there's any way Fuku-chan did.

00:17:08.180 --> 00:17:12.370
I want to say we rode as hard as we could.

00:17:12.370 --> 00:17:15.100
It was our last race.

00:17:15.100 --> 00:17:18.260
When I hear we lost by 
five or ten centimeters...

00:17:19.010 --> 00:17:21.230
In road racing, the difference
between first and second

00:17:21.230 --> 00:17:23.760
is the difference between heaven and earth.

00:17:23.760 --> 00:17:25.730
On top of that, it was the Inter-High.

00:17:25.730 --> 00:17:28.230
That's on a whole different level.

00:17:28.640 --> 00:17:34.440
And that inexperienced little 
airhead didn't understand that.

00:17:35.540 --> 00:17:38.620
No, he gave everything he had.

00:17:39.630 --> 00:17:44.250
He understood how important it was and 
rode with the greatest strength he had.

00:17:46.750 --> 00:17:48.740
We lost because...

00:17:49.320 --> 00:17:52.690
No, because I was naïve in my predictions.

00:17:56.750 --> 00:18:00.640
Number 176, Sohoku first-year Onoda...

00:18:00.640 --> 00:18:02.180
A total amateur.

00:18:02.660 --> 00:18:05.350
Though his face didn't show a 
shred of competitive spirit,

00:18:06.070 --> 00:18:12.070
hidden inside him was a determined 
and indomitable spirit.

00:18:12.070 --> 00:18:17.340
And that was enough to beat Hakone 
Academy's greatest climber, Manami.

00:18:18.810 --> 00:18:22.910
Manami said he was dangerous, 
but I couldn't predict it.

00:18:22.910 --> 00:18:24.730
That was only natural.

00:18:25.370 --> 00:18:31.540
He was the unpredictable element that 
Sohoku created during that race.

00:18:32.050 --> 00:18:33.960
That's not something which 
can be made on purpose.

00:18:34.610 --> 00:18:40.950
But it was the only way they 
could take down the champions.

00:18:41.640 --> 00:18:45.930
In other words, that's what
Kinjou was going for.

00:18:47.070 --> 00:18:48.690
Jin-kun said the same thing.

00:18:49.970 --> 00:18:50.810
Do you have a plan?

00:18:50.810 --> 00:18:52.190
Nope.

00:18:53.360 --> 00:18:57.360
For us, being connected to 
each other is important.

00:18:57.980 --> 00:19:00.110
<i>That four-eyes...</i>

00:19:00.110 --> 00:19:01.850
<i>Onoda-chan...</i>

00:19:02.930 --> 00:19:06.490
Isn't that why we need to show

00:19:06.040 --> 00:19:16.840
<b>Minegayama Hill Climb Race</b>

00:19:06.490 --> 00:19:11.090
the next generation of Hakone Academy how he rides?

00:19:11.930 --> 00:19:18.220
<i>We're here at the classic fall race, 
the Minegayama Hill Climb!</i>

00:19:18.220 --> 00:19:22.260
<i>The race starts here at Minegamachi, Chiba!</i>

00:19:20.430 --> 00:19:22.260
You can do it!

00:19:22.570 --> 00:19:23.710
Hey, look.

00:19:23.710 --> 00:19:26.500
It's the Inter-High general 
classification winner, Onoda.

00:19:28.140 --> 00:19:30.280
<i>Everyone's looking at me.</i>

00:19:30.280 --> 00:19:32.270
<i>Of course they are.</i>

00:19:33.000 --> 00:19:35.220
At the next Inter-High—no,

00:19:35.220 --> 00:19:39.610
starting with our next race,
the other teams will be gunning for us.

00:19:39.610 --> 00:19:42.910
We must leap past them and win again.

00:19:43.870 --> 00:19:46.830
Because we are the champions.

00:19:47.410 --> 00:19:50.270
<i>I'll win. I'll win.</i>

00:19:50.270 --> 00:19:53.120
<i>I have to win. I...</i>

00:19:55.560 --> 00:19:58.050
<i>What is winning?</i>

00:19:58.840 --> 00:20:01.550
<i>Pushing aside everyone here?</i>

00:20:02.820 --> 00:20:04.800
<i>Not losing to anyone else?</i>

00:20:05.340 --> 00:20:06.370
<i>I can't do it.</i>

00:20:06.780 --> 00:20:10.310
<i>I was able to ride in the Inter-High 
because the rest of the team was with me.</i>

00:20:11.110 --> 00:20:13.440
<i>I'm even weak during practice.</i>

00:20:13.940 --> 00:20:15.810
<i>My strength alone isn't enough.</i>

00:20:16.620 --> 00:20:17.500
Onoda...

00:20:19.890 --> 00:20:22.620
Team Sohoku supports each other.

00:20:23.130 --> 00:20:26.070
Sounds like something 
Kinjou-san would say, right?

00:20:26.870 --> 00:20:31.040
We can take it slow. Don't try 
to do everything yourself, Onoda.

00:20:32.220 --> 00:20:33.550
Teshima-san...

00:20:33.550 --> 00:20:34.920
He's right.

00:20:34.920 --> 00:20:38.530
We wouldn't want you getting 
overeager and falling again.

00:20:39.130 --> 00:20:40.380
Imaizumi-kun?

00:20:40.740 --> 00:20:45.110
Don't get so nervous
that you forget we're here.

00:20:45.580 --> 00:20:47.540
Just climb at your own pace.

00:20:47.990 --> 00:20:50.470
Even if you're late, we'll be 
waiting for you at the top.

00:20:53.220 --> 00:20:54.560
Okay.

00:20:59.740 --> 00:21:03.860
<i>Someone else will be 
participating in that race.</i>

00:21:04.670 --> 00:21:06.570
<i>This year's Inter-High champion,</i>

00:21:06.570 --> 00:21:08.370
Onoda-kun.

00:21:09.000 --> 00:21:10.320
Onoda?

00:21:10.320 --> 00:21:14.160
Ashikiba, experience what it's 
like to ride against him.

00:21:14.770 --> 00:21:16.570
And if possible, beat him.

00:21:17.380 --> 00:21:20.530
He was near the front, so I 
didn't get a good look at him.

00:21:22.170 --> 00:21:23.350
Well, whatever.

00:21:23.800 --> 00:21:26.390
I'll see what he can do during the race.

00:21:27.740 --> 00:21:28.900
Onoda-kun...

00:23:05.550 --> 00:23:07.390
Hello, everyone.

00:23:06.420 --> 00:23:10.660
<b>Makishima Yusuke</b>

00:23:07.390 --> 00:23:10.660
Today I'm going to show you 
how I make a spider pie.

00:23:11.010 --> 00:23:14.160
<b>Kitchen</b>

00:23:18.330 --> 00:23:19.460
Jeez!

00:23:22.210 --> 00:23:26.170
<b>Smile!!

00:23:22.680 --> 00:23:25.120
I can't believe you're 
crying already, Maki-chan.

00:23:25.120 --> 00:23:26.170
That voice!

00:23:26.650 --> 00:23:27.630
Toudou?

00:23:28.510 --> 00:23:30.340
Starting today...

00:23:31.400 --> 00:23:33.150
I'll be taking over this corner!

00:23:36.580 --> 00:23:39.980
<i>NEXT RIDE  Teshima's Ride of the Soul</i>

00:23:39.980 --> 00:23:44.980
